From f1a89997a67d829ddc05acc9561185e12fbb4745 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suifei <suifei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:39:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] serve(dsv41): read pictures with the model's own vision tower

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash is multimodal (config.json: image_token_id 129264,
vision_config with a 32-layer ViT, patch 14, merge 3, 1024 image tokens at
most) and the dsv41 engine carries that tower (src/dsv41/ds4_vision.cu) once
the pack is made with tools/dsv41/pack_gguf.py --mmproj.  Until now the
server's image path always went through the separate strata-vision encoder
(llama.cpp mtmd), which has no deepseek41v projector: the family was marked
images: false and --vision was ignored with a warning.

This teaches serve/server.py to use the engine's own tower for this family
instead:

* serve/dsv41_vision.py: the picture side - fit a picture to the tower's
  geometry (14-pixel patches, 3x3 merge, span <= max_image_tokens), the span
  one picture takes (rows = ceil(h/42) * (ceil(w/42) + 1) + 2, the formula
  the engine uses), the prompt markers, and the DSI1 pictures file a GENI
  request names (magic, count, start offset, width, height, RGB).
* server.py: Service(native_vision=...) - at prepare() the content lists are
  flattened to text with one marker per picture, the marker becomes a run of
  the image token before tokenizing, and the request's DSI1 file goes to the
  engine as GENI's pictures file; the encoder path is skipped, and
  /health, /metrics and /v1/models report image support.
* setup.py: the IST-DAS sets fetch mmproj-BF16.gguf (pinned) and pack it, and
  the family is marked vision: true.

Measured on 4x L20 (2.25 bpw, 1M context): 1008x672 -> 402 prompt tokens,
one word answer in 1.3 s; the tower encodes a picture in ~100 ms.
